From 1b7055e98923198550cf9caa98fb48c96ebc5b5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:13:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] GPU user space package sgx-ddk-um-n950; image: install it, no
 sphone, no rotation

sgx/build-deb.sh builds sgx-ddk-um-n950 from TI's omap5-sgx-ddk-um-linux
(1.17.4948957, ti335x, commit 84a396a, files checked against the ones
tested on the N950): TI's GPU libraries and pvrsrvctl for the SGX530 1.2.5
in place of sgx-ddk-um-ti343x's (dpkg-divert), Leste's libdbm kept, TI's
licence as the copyright file. Only tar, xz and ar are needed.

The image installs it, no longer starts sphone with the session (it
restarted itself in a loop without a modem) and turns hildon-desktop's
rotation off as leste-config-n900 does on the N900.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
